@startuml graph-model
' Ekte Mat Online — Neo4j graph model (Oblig 5; docs/plans/11-oblig5-neo4j.md).
' Boxes are node labels with their properties; arrows are relationship types (direction as stored).
' Implemented in app/models/repositories/neo4j/. Domain classes: domain-class.puml.
!pragma layout smetana
hide circle
hide methods
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor<<node>> #F5F9FF
  BackgroundColor<<fixed>> #F2F2F2
}

class User <<node>> {
  id : int {unique}
  email : string {unique, lower case}
  password_hash : string
  name : string
  phone : string [0..1]
  role : customer | admin
  created_at : LocalDateTime
}

class Order <<node>> {
  id : int {unique}
  order_number : "YY-NNNN" {unique}
  event_date : Date
  guest_count : int >= 1
  delivery_address : string
  status : OrderStatus
  payment_status : PaymentStatus
  created_at, updated_at : LocalDateTime
}

class OrderLine <<node>> {
  id : int {unique}
  item_name : string
  unit_price_nok : int > 0
  quantity : int >= 1
}

class GuestGroup <<node>> {
  id : int {unique}
  label : string
  count : int >= 1
  dietary_notes : string
}

class FoodItem <<node>> {
  id : int {unique}
  name : string
  description : string
  price_nok : int > 0
  min_order_qty : int >= 1
  published : boolean
  image_filename : string [0..1]
}

class EventCategory <<node>> {
  id : int {unique}
  slug : string {unique}
  name : string
  sort_order : int
}

class Question <<node>> {
  id : int {unique}
  text : string
  asked_at : LocalDateTime
  answer_text : string [0..1]
  answered_at : LocalDateTime [0..1]
}

class Allergen <<fixed>> {
  code : string {unique}
}

class DietaryLabel <<fixed>> {
  code : string {unique}
}

User "1" --> "0..*" Order : PLACED
Order "1" --> "1..*" OrderLine : HAS_LINE
OrderLine "0..*" --> "0..1" FoodItem : OF_ITEM
Order "1" --> "1..*" GuestGroup : HAS_GUEST_GROUP
GuestGroup "0..*" --> "0..*" Allergen : ALLERGIC_TO
FoodItem "0..*" --> "1..*" EventCategory : IN_CATEGORY
FoodItem "0..*" --> "0..*" Allergen : CONTAINS
FoodItem "0..*" --> "0..*" DietaryLabel : HAS_LABEL
User "1" --> "0..*" Question : ASKED
Question "0..*" --> "1" Order : ABOUT
User "0..1" --> "0..*" Question : ANSWERED

note bottom of Allergen
  14 EU allergens and 6 dietary labels are
  created once by init-db and shared, so
  "which ordered dishes contain an allergen
  a guest group has?" is one graph pattern:
  (:Order)-[:HAS_GUEST_GROUP]->()-[:ALLERGIC_TO]->(a)
  <-[:CONTAINS]-(f)<-[:OF_ITEM]-()<-[:HAS_LINE]-(:Order)
end note

note right of OrderLine
  name and price are copied at checkout;
  deleting a food item removes only OF_ITEM,
  the line keeps its history
end note

note as Tech
  Not domain data:
  (:Counter {name, value}) gives integer ids per label
  and order numbers per year; (:EkteMatSchema {version})
  marks an initialised database.
  Unique constraints on every {unique} property.
  Value rules (> 0, >= 1) are checked in the repositories
  (Community Edition has no value constraints).
end note
@enduml
